        "answer": {
          "short": "Asymptotes: $x=-1$, $y=2$. Intercepts: $(-\\frac12,0)$ and $(0,1)$.",
          "worked": "Reflect $y=\\frac1x$ across the $x$-axis, then translate left 1 unit and up 2 units. The asymptotes are $x=-1$ and $y=2$.\n\nAt $x=0$, $y=-\\frac1{0+1}+2=1$.\n\nFor the $x$-intercept:\n$$\\begin{align*}-\\frac1{x+1}+2&=0\\\\\\frac1{x+1}&=2\\\\x+1&=\\frac12\\\\x&=-\\frac12\\end{align*}$$\nThe intercepts are $(-\\frac12,0)$ and $(0,1)$.",
