          "short": "Asymptotes: $x=2$, $y=-1$. Intercepts: $(3,0)$ and $(0,-\\frac32)$.",
          "worked": "Translate $y=\\frac1x$ right 2 units and down 1 unit. The asymptotes are $x=2$ and $y=-1$.\n\nAt $x=0$, $y=\\frac1{0-2}-1=-\\frac32$.\n\nFor the $x$-intercept:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac1{x-2}-1&=0\\\\\\frac1{x-2}&=1\\\\x-2&=1\\\\x&=3\\end{align*}$$\nThe intercepts are $(3,0)$ and $(0,-\\frac32)$.",
